# Helios, the left branch of a ballot proof: the voter claims the vote
# was zero, so the ciphertext is (g^r0, h^r0).  Examples/Helios.v,
# ballot_stmt.
#
# The witness vector spans the whole disjunction, so this branch
# carries a column for r1 as well -- the randomness of the branch it
# is simulating.  It does not claim r1, and must not: a prover knows
# the randomness of only the branch that is true.  That is what
# Claim.live_claim computes, and dropping it is what turned 700 of 724
# leaves of a real election into false reports of degeneracy.
secrets r0 r1
claims  r0
eq  alpha   g  1
eq  beta    h  1
